AB  - Automatic modulation classification (AMC) plays a key role in intelligent wireless communication. AMC is widely used in civil and military field for its ability of identifying the modulation type of unknown signal without any prior knowledge. To improve the classification accuracy of feature based AMC at low signal-To-noise (SNR), a novel modulation classification scheme based on Variational Mode Decomposition (VMD) and multifractal analysis is proposed in this paper. The proposed scheme applies VMD to decompose the original signal into multiple intrinsic mode functions(IMFs). Then, multifractal analysis is used to extract multifractal features from each IMF, which combine with statistical features extracted from each IMF as the input of Extreme Learning Machine (ELM). In this paper, we use SMW200A Vector Signal Generator to generate real RF data to verify the effectiveness of the proposed scheme, and simulate the additive white Gaussian noise (AWGN) to verify the robustness of the scheme to noise. The results show that the proposed scheme can reach an average accuracy of 95% when the SNR is 0dB. © 2020 IEEE.
